Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:24:55 +0000
Subject: Send a reduced Accept-Language header

Enable the ReduceAcceptLanguage feature. navigator.languages now exposes
only the first language of the user's list, the same one that
navigator.language already reports in this browser. The Accept-Language
header carries a single language instead of the full list: by default
that first language, and for an origin that announced its languages, the
language that the browser negotiated and stored for it. When a site lists
the languages it offers in an Avail-Language response header and the
first language is not among them, the browser picks the best match from
the rest of the user's list, restarts the navigation once with it, and
remembers the choice for that origin for 30 days. For such an origin the
header and navigator.languages name different languages. The full language
list is a stable fingerprinting signal sent to every server, and this
reduces it to one value. GrapheneOS Vanadium uses the same default.

